use ../lib/Operator

export operator DupMergeOperator:
    description:
        The `++` operator is like merge, but it keeps duplicates.

        On lists it joins them in order and keeps everything, so
        `[A, B, C, D] ++ [A, B, C]` gives you `[A, B, C, D, A, B, C]`.

        On dictionaries it's a deep merge. If both sides have the same key and
        both values are dictionaries, those get merged too, all the way down.
        Otherwise the right side wins.

        On strings it joins them with a line break.

    symbol: ++
